============================================================
 CYBERSECURITY MULTI-AGENT INFRASTRUCTURE - SETUP GUIDE
============================================================

This program relies on three different programming languages and native OS networking tools. Please follow these steps carefully to set up your environment.

------------------------------------------------------------
 PART 1: SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS & PREREQUISITES
------------------------------------------------------------
1. Operating System: Windows 10/11 (Recommended for full GUI and netsh firewall features).
2. Administrator Privileges: You MUST have Admin rights to capture packets and modify firewall rules.

------------------------------------------------------------
 PART 2: DOWNLOAD CORE COMPILERS & ENGINES
------------------------------------------------------------
You must download and install the following toolchains:

1. Python (3.9 or higher): 
   - Download: https://www.python.org/downloads/
   - IMPORTANT: Check the box that says "Add Python to PATH" during installation.

2. Go (Golang):
   - Download: https://go.dev/dl/
   - Follow the default installation instructions.

3. Rust & Cargo:
   - Download: https://rustup.rs/
   - Download and run `rustup-init.exe`. Follow the default prompts to install the Rust compiler and Cargo package manager.

4. Nmap (Network Mapper):
   - Download: https://nmap.org/download.html
   - Install it and ensure Nmap is added to your system PATH. 
   - NOTE: The installer usually includes Npcap. Make sure to check "Install Npcap in WinPcap API-compatible Mode".

5. Npcap SDK (For compiling the Rust sniffer):
   - Download: https://npcap.com/#download
   - Look for the "Npcap SDK" zip file.
   - Extract the zip file and rename the folder to exactly "npcap-sdk".
   - Place this "npcap-sdk" folder directly into the root directory of this project.

------------------------------------------------------------
 PART 3: INSTALL PYTHON DEPENDENCIES
------------------------------------------------------------
Open your Command Prompt or PowerShell and run the following command to install the required Python UI and networking libraries:

    pip install customtkinter Pillow requests dnspython

------------------------------------------------------------
 PART 4: COMPILE THE BACKEND ENGINES
------------------------------------------------------------
Open your terminal and navigate to the folder where you extracted this project.

1. Compile the Go Engine:
   Run the following command in the root of the project:
   
       go build -o SecurityScanner.exe main.go

   (This will create the SecurityScanner.exe file that the Python UI needs).

2. Build the Rust Engine:
   Ensure your `npcap-sdk` folder is in the root directory, then run:

       cargo build --release

   (This ensures all crates like pcap, etherparse, and rusqlite download and compile successfully).

------------------------------------------------------------
 PART 5: RUNNING THE APPLICATION
------------------------------------------------------------
Because this tool intercepts raw network traffic and manipulates the host firewall, it CANNOT be run as a normal user.

1. Open your Start Menu, type "cmd" or "powershell".
2. Right-click it and select "Run as Administrator".
3. Navigate to the project folder (e.g., `cd C:\path\to\project`).
4. Launch the dashboard:

       python dashboard.py

The holographic UI will load, and your worker agents are now ready to scan and defend your network.
